European human rights law, particularly as articulated in the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR), recognizes the right to freedom of assembly as a fundamental human right. Article 11 of the ECHR guarantees this right, allowing individuals and groups to gather peacefully to express their views. However, this right is not absolute and can be subject to certain restrictions, particularly when it comes to considerations for public order, safety, and the rights of others.

